Corrected message:

Let text and shape rows be dragged onto another layer

A text or shape row in the Layers panel can be dropped onto another
layer's row, its mask row, or between its object rows to move the
object to that layer. The object keeps its position on the canvas, and
the move is a single undo step that re-renders both layers.

Modifier rows stay on their own layer. Dragging a row that can't move
is refused at the start, so the pointer shows it can't drop instead of
the drag silently doing nothing.
